  <document-link format="APPLICATION/PDF" url="https://aidstream.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/documents/1_Baseline-report-final-compressed-20220803010847.pdf">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">VCA Baseline report 2021</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Voices for Just Climate Action (VCA) is a five-year programme funded by the Netherlands Ministry of Foreign Affairs under the &#x2018;Power of Voices&#x2019; framework and being implemented by an Alliance comprising of strong Southern CSOs &#x2013; Akina Mama wa Afrika (AMwA), Fundaci&#xf3;n Avina, Slum Dwellers International (SDI) and SouthSouthNorth (SSN) &#x2013; and two Global CSOs &#x2013; Hivos and WWF-Netherlands. The programme is being implemented in Bolivia &amp; Paraguay, Brazil, Indonesia, Kenya, Tunisia, Zambia and is supported by a global programme and a Dutch society engagement component. Our five-year strategic objective is that: &#x201c;By 2025, local civil society groups have claimed a central role as empowered innovators, facilitators and advocates of climate solutions&#x201d;.This report is the result of individual country baseline studies carried out by the Alliance partners, and a concerted effort to draw cross-cutting insights and consolidate these into one baseline report. The country baseline studies have been executed between June and September 2021 and aimed specifically to update context information of the situation between January and June 2021.</narrative>
   </description>
